    "lessonTitle": "Lesson 23.1: Nuclear Radiation",
    "type": "numerical",
    "difficulty": "honors",
    "angle": "quantitative_conservation",
    "question": "In a closed, conservative state transformation for \"Nuclear Radiation\", the conjugate state variables satisfy the invariant balance relation: $$X_1 \\times Y_1 = X_2 \\times Y_2$$ Given initial conditions $X_1 = 25.0$ and $Y_1 = 14.0$, if parameter $X$ is perturbed to $X_2 = 27.0$, calculate the resulting conjugate parameter $Y_2$ to three significant figures.",
    "correctAnswer": "12.96",
    "tolerance": 0.1,
    "unit": "kJ/mol",
    "options": [
      "$9.72\\text{ kJ/mol}$",
      "$19.44\\text{ kJ/mol}$",
      "$12.96\\text{ kJ/mol}$",
      "$16.20\\text{ kJ/mol}$"
    ],
